menu "Wi-Fi debug"

    config WIFI_DEBUG_SSID
        string "Network to join"
        default ""
        help
            The Wi-Fi network the unit joins when Wi-Fi debug is switched
            on in the settings screen. Can be changed from the web page,
            which keeps its own copy in NVS. Empty: go straight to the
            unit's own access point.

    config WIFI_DEBUG_PASSWORD
        string "Password for that network"
        default ""

    config WIFI_DEBUG_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Password for the unit's own access point"
        default "miniefis"
        help
            Used when the network above cannot be joined. At least 8
            characters (WPA2); anything shorter leaves the access point
            open, and with it the firmware upload.

endmenu

menu "Compass"

    config MAG_DIP_DEG
        int "Magnetic dip where the unit is used, degrees"
        range -90 90
        default 67
        help
            The angle the earth's field points down into the ground,
            positive north of the equator: 67 across Poland, 64-68 over
            most of Europe. A world magnetic model gives it for anywhere.
            The compass swing cannot measure the vertical magnetometer
            offset, and takes it from this instead: a degree out costs a
            couple of degrees of heading at 20 degrees of bank, nothing
            level.

endmenu
